  {
   "key": "similar",
   "title": "Diseases that share the same biology",
   "text": "Krabbe disease shares the same type of nerve-coating damage, called demyelination, as MLD [Ecba7ed0, E8b1c4df]. Krabbe disease also involves a buildup of fatty substances and a missing lysosomal enzyme, the same pattern seen in MLD [E3f6bbf0, Eecc2812, E60744b8, E25007cf, E7ba2aee, E7ee77ad, Ee586157, E050a41e, E2774850, E405f851]. Both MLD and Krabbe disease show higher protein levels in spinal fluid, nerve-coating damage outside the brain, and slower nerve signals, according to HPO [E1e675ab, E8f41824, Ed4f35c8, Ea2c011c, E3abe212, E13dd0cf]. Gaucher disease also involves the same fatty buildup and missing lysosomal enzyme pattern as MLD [Ec8d1187, E96ea7eb, Eb29eb38, E309fa8a, E4cac688, E28eb929, E8ace403, Ed59ee48], and both conditions are passed down in the same autosomal recessive way, according to HPO [E791ca08, E4180b6b]. Fabry disease shares the same fatty buildup and missing lysosomal enzyme pattern too [Ee0e2214, E5b662da, E2cdb1f6, E4442b91, E5f25d91, E487816a, E871c351, Ef74cc75, E4b5796e, E7328024, Eb305e87, E81c4573, E58d2a7e, E3b56952, E66d6b66, E7dab347, E1577d5e], and both MLD and Fabry disease can include seizures, according to HPO [Ed052fd9, Efee1024]. Parkinson's disease that starts later in life shares the same fatty buildup and enzyme shortage pattern, linked to a gene called GBA1 [E8b12886, Eb9285bb, Ece278e5, E2361d59, E6d3e762, Ec180f15], and both MLD and this form of Parkinson's disease can include hallucinations, muscle tightening called dystonia, and trouble speaking called dysarthria, according to HPO [E282b01f, Eb5cebaa, E8e4cedd, Ea493fb5, Ed944d8b, E166e701].",
