  {
   "key": "what_exists",
   "title": "What already exists",
   "text": "A patient group called the MLD Foundation, based in the United States, works with families affected by MLD [Ef09b1a9, E191273d]. A patient group called the MPS Society, based in the United Kingdom, also works on MLD [E1dfdb85, Ecfa62ac, E4ac6cf1]. A group called the MLD initiative, based in the Netherlands, runs an international registry for MLD [Ec750679, E0dd2ea1, E8156254]. According to ClinicalTrials.gov, a completed study tested a medicine called SHP611 in children with MLD, run by Shire [E928a58f, Eaab309d, E88a4ad3]. According to ClinicalTrials.gov, the Shenzhen Geno-Immune Medical Institute has two gene therapy studies for MLD that are not yet recruiting, both based in China [Ee28d284, Ea6a0efe, E8234b12, E66bddab]. According to ClinicalTrials.gov, Albert Einstein College of Medicine runs a newborn screening study in the United States that includes MLD [E2523361, E788b2ff]. According to ClinicalTrials.gov, a study led by Joanne Kurtzberg, MD is recruiting in the United States to look at a cell transplant approach for MLD and related diseases [E478a4f9, E563dd91].",
